    <string name="admin_confirm_title">Confirm device change</string>
    <string name="admin_confirm_step">Changing the position multiplier changes physical movement per UI step and can invalidate the displayed position. EAFCON blocks movement until you reset the position display and set a new software limit. Continue?</string>
    <string name="admin_confirm_sync">This changes the number displayed as the current position without moving the focuser. Confirm that the entered value matches the physical focuser state.</string>
    <string name="admin_confirm_max">This changes the controller travel limit. Keep a safe travel margin and confirm the exact value. The new maximum cannot be below the current position or software limit.</string>
    <string name="admin_confirm_coil">OFF immediately releases idle holding torque, so gravity or a mechanical load may move the focuser. ON keeps holding torque while idle but increases power use and heat. Apply this change?</string>
    <string name="admin_confirm_home">The Home command may move the focuser. Keep the travel path clear. The protocol does not acknowledge completion, so EAFCON cannot confirm where it stopped. Continue?</string>
    <string name="admin_confirm_celsius">Send the one-way command to set the controller temperature display to Celsius? The protocol has no readback.</string>
    <string name="admin_confirm_temperature_unit">Change the temperature unit stored by the controller? EAFCON will read the setting back before confirming.</string>
